vents","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":653,"digest":"sha256:dc7881910995db40136030491ce3fff560e05c40bf66b446ed630502624e4a07","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-16T22:40:26Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T22:40:26Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m127-v0.12.7/m12stage7-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m127-v0.12.7","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m127-v0.12.7","body":"# Engacer OS M12.7 / 0.12.7 - File commands and transfers\n\nNative qualification passes **M12-STAGE7-VM-v1**.\n[Exact-source acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a7a6c1fb49414ad140741b7d1e4a0ce5dcac9d0d/evidence/M12/7/acceptance-results.json) verifies\n584 compiled Git inputs, fourteen native journeys, real 150%/4K, twelve cached/full\ncomparisons, matching VMware/BIOS setup and ordinary starts. Actual slot recovery\nrestores damaged owned BIOS boot bytes and starts independently. Public release,\nindependent downloads and complete website verification close separately.\n\nBuild: `595e94df44cc995c3379d11379f4663e`.\nISO SHA256: `11832944be106bfa560856f4978994a59e17613ddc0c283c1704816e7ff041f2`.\nVMware ZIP SHA256: `addfc2f971b5de5407318706febbc73cf69c56df68a1eba741417bb494581476`.\n\n## What changes\n\nThe common toolbar and right-click routes share command capability checks.\nActions remains visible at the real 500x420 minimum, including Copy/Cut/Paste,\nRename, Recycle, New folder/text, Undo, Properties and last-transfer details.\nSystem protections, busy guards and owner checks remain effective through keys.\n\nUSB Copy to Downloads shares the checked cooperative job and conflict review\nwith Copy/Paste. A single generation-bound lease reads at most 4096 bytes per\nstep into the existing buffer. Physically consecutive clusters are coalesced\nonly after their FAT links are checked; fragmented and unaligned reads preserve\nactual order. A 1,568-byte metadata cache avoids repeated mirrored FAT reads.\n\nProgress shows the phase, source and destination, with Cancel and confirmed work.\nMinimizing the owner retains global progress and Cancel above the taskbar.\nOnly the progress strip is damaged during steady work. Completed, cancelled and\nstopped jobs retain Details. Native Keep both/Skip/Replace, single-action Undo,\nRecycle/Restore, protected locations and partial tree cancellation are checked.\nAn unfinished destination stream is not published; completed items remain.\n\nThe live installer now independently compresses nonzero pages using the checked\nbounded private record codec. The loader correctly refused an earlier candidate\nthat crossed firmware-owned ACPI NVS at 8 MiB; memory ownership checks remain\nintact. The final live ELF stays below that boundary. Install/recovery decode\nand validate complete pages before destination I/O; a build guard rejects a\nfuture oversized fixed-address image. Installed BIOS layout remains compact.\nUse the matching recovery ISO; older media cannot replay new encoded records.\nThis does not implement arbitrary firmware placement or universal boot support.\n\n[Architecture and choices](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a7a6c1fb49414ad140741b7d1e4a0ce5dcac9d0d/docs/architecture/transfers-m127.md),\n[commands and transfers guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a7a6c1fb49414ad140741b7d1e4a0ce5dcac9d0d/docs/handbook/transfers-m127.md),\n[eight-step installation](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a7a6c1fb49414ad140741b7d1e4a0ce5dcac9d0d/docs/handbook/install-m127.md).\n\n## Qualification and limits\n\nActual native testing checks a 64-MiB USB copy, cancellation after reading began,\nbackground feedback, native partial completion, source removal and independent\nfull payload/CRC comparison. The original 1-GiB USB fixture remains unchanged.\nThe codec host tests check 544 real/generated pages and 10,808 malformed/fuzz\ncases with unchanged output guards. Native compressed-slot replay independently\nrestores deliberately corrupted owned boot bytes and starts without the ISO.\n\nThe production old/new FAT32 reader host comparison needs 13.57 times fewer I/O\nrequests for the same bytes. This is a request-count comparison, not physical\nthroughput or hardware FPS. The 18.5-second native full-copy observer interval\nalso includes test input; it is not a storage benchmark.\n\nFixed shell state stays **545,636 bytes**. Fixed FAT32 state is **9,920 bytes**,\n**1,696 above M12.6**, including the 1,568-byte cache. No new persistent payload\nbuffer is added. Managed pages return to **4,288,512 bytes**, peak **4,337,664**,\nwith zero retained pages/new allocation failures and halted idle CPUs.\n[Resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a7a6c1fb49414ad140741b7d1e4a0ce5dcac9d0d/evidence/M12/7/resources.json) distinguish those values from\nconfigured RAM, live linked ranges and font/device/framebuffer storage.\n\nUSB imports remain one-file and at most 64 MiB. Export remains synchronous,\ncreate-only and cannot be cancelled mid-file. USB folders, Cut/Move, overwrite,\nformat expansion and sorting remain unavailable. Rename/move/recycle clears the\nfile clipboard under the retained move policy; Copy/Cut again before Paste.\n\nShared-menu footer fitting and more specific conflict name/provider feedback\nremain M12.14; the earlier HiDPI cursor observation remains M12.16. The earlier\nconcurrent BIOS/AHCI timeout is retained for M12.18; stress reliability remains\nunqualified. Final controller/device/original-app regression is M12.18. Physical,\nARM, vendor GPU 3D and universal DOS/Windows compatibility are not claimed.\nAgent visual/scenario review is distinct from a human usability study.\n\n![Actual native USB transfer](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/a7a6c1fb49414ad140741b7d1e4a0ce5dcac9d0d/evidence/M12/7/feature.png)\n"}